  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Nairobi 1% Workplan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">As non-resident agency, and because of the complex nature of Somalia&#x2019;s security and political environment, UNESCO&#x2019;s capacity to meaningfully engage in the country has been limited, and programmes and activities often of an ad hoc and fragmented nature. The Somali authorities view with concern this lack of engagement and responsiveness to needs and requests for assistance.

The development of a new UNSDCF (2026-2030), as well as confirmed funding interest from the Peacebuilding Fund (PBF) for a UNESCO-UNICEF Joint Programme on Peace Education (budget: USD 2.5 million) supported by the UN Resident Coordinator, provide a concrete opportunity for UNESCO to develop a more strategic cooperation with and in Somalia.</narrative>
  </description>
